  "published": "2026-11-13T15:37:08.71Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "A region you list is a language of its own to the build. With en-GB next to en in [assembly: SupportedLanguages], every contract of the assembly needs a set for en-GB (LOC004), as every inline text already takes enGB:. The error names the set to add, such as 'class ShopTranslationsEnGB : ShopTranslationsEN', which can add nothing. To give one contract British wording and leave the rest alone, keep en-GB out of the attribute and implement LanguageCode in that set.\n\nUnchanged: a library's set covers the regions of its language. An app that lists en-GB owes a library with an English set no British one.\n\nThe docs and the messages of the build now show a region as British English next to English.",
